{"type":"WebSearch","query":"California Proposition 42 election results early returns November 3 2026","content":"**As of the latest unofficial updates (around November 2–3, 2026), there are no reported votes or precincts for California Proposition 42.** The California Secretary of State’s election results site shows 0.0% of precincts reporting (0 of ~23,860), with 0 yes votes and 0 no votes. CNN’s live results page similarly shows 0% in. Polls close at 8 p.m. Pacific Time on Election Day (November 3, 2026), after which unofficial election-night results will begin appearing. Results will continue updating during the canvass period (certified by December 11, 2026) as mail, provisional, and other ballots are counted.[[1]](https://electionresults.sos.ca.gov/returns/ballot-measures/county)

Proposition 42 (an initiated constitutional amendment) would prohibit new state taxes (enacted on or after January 1, 2026) on the ownership or control of personal property, including retirement holdings, savings, investments, and other non-real-estate assets, as well as certain retroactive taxes. It includes a competing-measures provision that could nullify Proposition 40 (the “billionaire tax”) if both pass but Prop 42 receives more votes. It does not affect existing taxes or real property taxes.[[2]](https://ballotpedia.org/California_Proposition_42,_Prohibit_New_Taxes_on_Retirement_Holdings,_Personal_Assets,_and_Savings_and_Limit_Retroactive_Taxes_Initiative_(2026))

Live unofficial results (statewide and by county) are available on the California Secretary of State site (electionresults.sos.ca.gov) and major outlets like CNN once reporting begins. Early/mail ballot turnout statewide was already high heading into Election Day (over 6 million ballots returned by November 2), but this does not include proposition-specific vote splits. Check official sources for the most current figures, as they will change.","citations":["https://electionresults.sos.ca.gov/returns/ballot-measures/county","https://ballotpedia.org/California_Proposition_42,_Prohibit_New_Taxes_on_Retirement_Holdings,_Personal_Assets,_and_Savings_and_Limit_Retroactive_Taxes_Initiative_(2026)"],"allowed_domains":null}
